; Interprets: RFC 7155
;; What RFC 7155's clauses state in prose about an AVP's value or presence,
;; read by hand and pinned to the sentences read (docs/constraints.md), in
;; clause order. The document obsoletes RFC 4005, whose own file reads its
;; text; where it repeats RFC 4005, its file quotes its own. A block with no
;; scope, or within a grouped AVP, holds wherever a document reading RFC
;; 7155's AVP reads it; a block on a command binds RFC 7155's own print of
;; the command, which no other document's print shares (docs/constraints.md,
;; Precedence). What a NAS or server decides and an earlier message are not
;; in the message, so a rule resting on them is `text-only`.


;; The four requests the section lists, each the document's own print;
;; section 1.4's CER is RFC 6733's command, which this file does not print.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: aar-auth-application-id-nasreq
; AVP: Auth-Application-Id
; Command: AA-Request
; Section: 1.5
"When used in this application, the Auth-Application-Id AVP MUST be set to the value one (1) in the following messages"
"o AA-Request (Section 3.1)"
    range 1


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: rar-auth-application-id-nasreq
; AVP: Auth-Application-Id
; Command: Re-Auth-Request
; Section: 1.5
"When used in this application, the Auth-Application-Id AVP MUST be set to the value one (1) in the following messages"
"o Re-Auth-Request(Section 3.3)"
    range 1


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: str-auth-application-id-nasreq
; AVP: Auth-Application-Id
; Command: Session-Termination-Request
; Section: 1.5
"When used in this application, the Auth-Application-Id AVP MUST be set to the value one (1) in the following messages"
"o Session-Termination-Request (Section 3.5)"
    range 1


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: asr-auth-application-id-nasreq
; AVP: Auth-Application-Id
; Command: Abort-Session-Request
; Section: 1.5
"When used in this application, the Auth-Application-Id AVP MUST be set to the value one (1) in the following messages"
"o Abort-Session-Request (Section 3.7)"
    range 1


;; The State AVPs of the AA-Answer before, an earlier message.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: aar-state-from-the-aaa
; AVP: State
; Command: AA-Request
; Section: 3.1
"A subsequent AAR message SHOULD be sent, with the User-Password AVP that includes the user's response to the prompt and MUST include any State AVPs that were present in the AAA message."
    text-only


;; The QoSFilterRule's text, with section 4.4.9's options, which no codec
;; reads.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: qos-filter-rule-format
; AVP: QoS-Filter-Rule
; Section: 4.1.1
"QoSFilterRule filters MUST follow the following format:"
    text-only


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: originating-line-info-octets
; AVP: Originating-Line-Info
; Section: 4.2.8
"The Value field contains two octets (00 - 99)."
    length 2 octets


;; The AVP carries the clear text: the encryption is the transport's, IPsec
;; or TLS, as the clause says before.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: user-password-length
; AVP: User-Password
; Section: 4.3.1
"The clear-text password (prior to encryption) MUST NOT be longer than 128 bytes in length."
    length *..128 octets


;; The AA-Request is the one command of the document printing CHAP-Auth.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: aar-chap-auth-with-challenge
; AVP: CHAP-Auth
; Command: AA-Request
; Section: 4.3.4
"If the CHAP-Auth AVP is found in a message, the CHAP-Challenge AVP (Section 4.3.8) MUST be present as well."
    requires CHAP-Challenge


;; CHAP with MD5 (5), the one value the clause defines.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: chap-auth-md5-response
; AVP: CHAP-Response
; Within: CHAP-Auth
; Section: 4.3.5
"This algorithm requires that the CHAP-Response AVP (Section 4.3.7) MUST be present in the CHAP-Auth AVP (Section 4.3.4)."
    present-if CHAP-Algorithm = "CHAP with MD5"


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: chap-ident-octet
; AVP: CHAP-Ident
; Section: 4.3.6
"The CHAP-Ident AVP (AVP Code 404) is of type OctetString and contains the 1 octet CHAP Identifier used in the computation of the CHAP response [RFC1994]."
    length 1 octets


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: chap-response-octets
; AVP: CHAP-Response
; Section: 4.3.7
"The CHAP-Response AVP (AVP Code 405) is of type OctetString and contains the 16-octet authentication data provided by the user in response to the CHAP challenge [RFC1994]."
    length 16 octets


;; The AA-Request is the one command of the document printing the three;
;; the clause's "is only present when the Framed-Protocol AVP ... is set to
;; ARAP" has no MUST, and is not read.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: aar-arap-password-without-other-passwords
; AVP: ARAP-Password
; Command: AA-Request
; Section: 4.3.9
"This AVP MUST NOT be present if either the User-Password or the CHAP-Auth AVP is present."
    excludes User-Password or CHAP-Auth


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: arap-challenge-response-octets
; AVP: ARAP-Challenge-Response
; Section: 4.3.10
"This AVP contains an 8-octet response to the dial-in client's challenge."
    length 8 octets


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: framed-mtu-range
; AVP: Framed-MTU
; Section: 4.4.10.3
"The MTU value MUST be in the range from 64 to 65535."
    range 64..65535


;; An IPv4 address, four octets, as RADIUS's attribute carries it.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: framed-ip-address-octets
; AVP: Framed-IP-Address
; Section: 4.4.10.5.1
"The Framed-IP-Address AVP (AVP Code 8) [RFC2865] is of type OctetString and contains an IPv4 address of the type specified in the attribute value to be configured for the user."
    length 4 octets


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: framed-ip-netmask-octets
; AVP: Framed-IP-Netmask
; Section: 4.4.10.5.2
"The Framed-IP-Netmask AVP (AVP Code 9) is of type OctetString and contains the four octets of the IPv4 netmask to be configured for the user when the user is a router to a network."
    length 4 octets


;; The request's OctetString's value, which no condition reads.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: aaa-framed-ip-netmask-after-all-ones
; AVP: Framed-IP-Netmask
; Command: AA-Answer
; Section: 4.4.10.5.2
"This AVP MUST be present in a response if the request included this AVP with a value of 0xFFFFFFFF."
    text-only


;; A route's text, which no codec reads.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: framed-route-text
; AVP: Framed-Route
; Section: 4.4.10.5.3
"The string MUST contain a destination prefix in dotted quad form optionally followed by a slash and a decimal-length specifier stating how many high-order bits of the prefix should be used."
    text-only


;; As Framed-Route's.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: framed-ipv6-route-text
; AVP: Framed-IPv6-Route
; Section: 4.4.10.5.7
"The string MUST contain an IPv6 address prefix followed by a slash and a decimal-length specifier stating how many high-order bits of the prefix should be used."
    text-only


;; The values the clause defines. Its "MUST only be present in an
;; authorization response" is table 5.1's AA-Request "0", read there, and
;; the Accounting-Request's body prints the AVP (docs/constraints.md).
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: framed-appletalk-link-range
; AVP: Framed-Appletalk-Link
; Section: 4.4.10.7.1
"Despite the size of the field, values range from 0 to 65,535."
    range 0..65535


;; As Framed-Appletalk-Link's.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: framed-appletalk-network-range
; AVP: Framed-Appletalk-Network
; Section: 4.4.10.7.2
"Despite the size of the field, values range from 0 to 65,535."
    range 0..65535


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: login-tcp-port-range
; AVP: Login-TCP-Port
; Section: 4.4.11.4.1
"The value MUST NOT be greater than 65,535."
    range 0..65535


; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: aaa-login-lat-service-for-lat
; AVP: Login-LAT-Service
; Command: AA-Answer
; Section: 4.4.11.5.1
"This AVP MUST only be present in the response if the Login-Service AVP states that LAT is desired."
    requires Login-Service = LAT


;; The clause's Login-Service-Type is section 4.4.11.3's Login-Service.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: aaa-login-lat-node-for-lat
; AVP: Login-LAT-Node
; Command: AA-Answer
; Section: 4.4.11.5.2
"This AVP MUST only be present in a response if the Login-Service-Type AVP is set to LAT."
    requires Login-Service = LAT


;; As section 4.4.11.5.2's.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: aaa-login-lat-group-for-lat
; AVP: Login-LAT-Group
; Command: AA-Answer
; Section: 4.4.11.5.3
"This AVP MUST only be present in a response if the Login-Service-Type AVP is set to LAT."
    requires Login-Service = LAT


;; As section 4.4.11.5.2's.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: aaa-login-lat-port-for-lat
; AVP: Login-LAT-Port
; Command: AA-Answer
; Section: 4.4.11.5.4
"This AVP MUST only be present in a response if the Login-Service-Type AVP is set to LAT."
    requires Login-Service = LAT


;; Whether a name other than the default is desired is the server's.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: tunnel-client-auth-id-other-than-default
; AVP: Tunnel-Client-Auth-Id
; Within: Tunneling
; Section: 4.5.10
"This AVP MUST be present in the authorization response if an authentication name other than the default is desired."
    text-only


;; As section 4.5.10's.
; Type: Interpreted Constraints
; Id: tunnel-server-auth-id-other-than-default
; AVP: Tunnel-Server-Auth-Id
; Within: Tunneling
; Section: 4.5.11
"This AVP MUST be present in the authorization response if an authentication name other than the default is desired."
    text-only


;; Table 5.1's AAR column: what its "0" says the AA-Request never
